# Phase Gates

Before writing code, read `docs/CURRENT_PHASE.md` and `docs/phase-gates.md`. Work only on the current phase. Do not start the next phase until every checkbox in the current phase is true.

Build the financial mechanism first. Frontend comes after the loop works. The failure mode is a beautiful dashboard that does not control capital.

Literal first sequence: Credit Vault → Credit Account → Trading Policy → Basic Trade Execution → Credit Score Engine → Adaptive Risk Engine → Policy Controller → Frontend → Stress Simulation → Polish + Demo.

Do not open VS Code and implement all six contracts on day one. Sprint 1: repo + Foundry/Next/FastAPI + Monad env → Registry + Vault + tests → TradingAccount + tests → RiskPolicy/Controller + tests → simple execution + onchain reject → DB + ingest + initial scoring.

Definition of done: LP deposits USDC → trader receives history-based credit → onchain trade → market risk rises → Kredxo reduces credit/policy → the smart contract rejects a now-over-limit trade → market recovers → credit increases again. Real Monad transactions.

If asked to add features, map them to a phase and priority. Refuse out-of-scope work that would skip a gate.
